[
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Field/TransferInstance.lean</code> has this definition of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Equiv.normedField#doc\">docs#Equiv.normedField</a> :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Equiv</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Transfer a `NormedField` across an `Equiv` -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">normedField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">field</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induced</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ringEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">injective</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Equiv</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I was reviewing <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41543\">#41543</a> which uses this to transfer a normed field structure along a bijection like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Completion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fast_instance</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">equivCompletion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">normedField</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and looking at <code>#print foo</code> I see a whole bunch of stuff which looks like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">div</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">equivCompletion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">equivCompletion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">equivCompletion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a_1</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and this looks good to me, and then at the end I see this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a_1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">UniformSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Completion</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extension₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">equivCompletion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ringEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">equivCompletion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ringEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a_1</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and this just looks totally different to all the other instances, it is making a ringEquiv, it is not using this <code>.toFun</code> and <code>.invFun</code> trick which is used everywhere else -- is this an issue?</p>",
